rage after a period of vacancy. Check your policy and gather records of how the home was winterized."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How do insurers separate wind and flood damage on Lake Erie?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Flood and surface water are excluded from homeowners policies, while wind damage is commonly covered. Insurers look at water lines, debris and the pattern of damage. A clear, room-by-room record helps show what wind caused."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can limestone and brick buildings near downtown Sandusky be repaired to match?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Often, but matching old stone and mortar takes skilled masons and specific materials. A good estimate accounts for that labor and material, rather than pricing the work as standard brick repair."}}],"@id":"https://ohioinsuranceappraiser.com/service-cities/sandusky-ohio/#faq"},{"@type":"Service","name":"Insurance appraisal in Sandusky, Ohio","serviceType":"Insurance appraisal","description":"Insurance appraiser in Sandusky, Ohio for Lake Erie wind, winter and water claims in Erie County. Independent estimates for homes and rentals.","provider":{"@id":"https://ohioinsuranceappraiser.com/#business"},"areaServed":{"@type":"City","name":"Sandusky","containedInPlace":{"@type":"State","name":"Ohio"}},"url":"https://ohioinsuranceappraiser.com/service-cities/sandusky-ohio/","@id":"https://ohioinsuranceappraiser.com/service-cities/sandusky-ohio/#service"}]}</script>
